<!--
   Data extraction rules for API 31+ (backup_rules.xml covers API 30 and below).

   Nothing has to be excluded, from cloud backup or from device transfer. The optional PP-OCRv6
   Medium model is no longer app data at all: it lives in Google Play's asset-pack storage and Gaten
   only reads it (ocr/PpOcrPack.kt), so the in-app model directory the removed downloader wrote — and
   the exclusion that used to name it — are gone. What stays app-owned is small and outside Android's
   backup by construction: the WaniKani token and its cache sit under noBackupFilesDir, which is never
   backed up or transferred.

   The file stays because the manifest points at it; empty rule sets mean the platform's defaults,
   which is what this app wants.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup />
    <device-transfer />
</data-extraction-rules>
